The live source check supports keeping the legal rows verified, but the Commission examples need their own receipt or removal. I’ll remove that nonessential example and narrow the commercial model: CRA is the recurring offer; Data Act becomes a separately priced implementation module with its own product buyer. That resolves both budget ownership and the missing competitor category without pretending there is one combined buyer.
