-<li><strong>Days 46–75:</strong> deliver at most two paid baselines in the customer's existing tools. Time every task and mark each decision as legal, manufacturer risk, technical implementation or routine operation. Run the incident clock and one data-access path with real product evidence.</li>
-<li><strong>Days 76–90:</strong> ask each buyer to sign a six-month managed-operation pilot at €3,000 a month, billed monthly in advance. The pass rule is two paid baselines from ten qualified offers and at least one retainer signed, with 60% of forecast recurring work classed as analyst/engineer work rather than founder judgement. The kill rule is no paid baseline after ten qualified offers, or two baselines that expose less than one day a month of recurring external work.</li>
+<li><strong>Days 1–15:</strong> choose only connected food and packaging machinery OEMs. Screen twenty accounts for own-brand products, controlled software releases, field support and no dedicated product-security operation. Secure one product-security lawyer and one machinery/CE adviser to review boundaries.</li>
+<li><strong>Days 16–30:</strong> conduct ten 45-minute English-language workflow interviews with engineering and quality leaders. Reconstruct the last release, vulnerability and customer security request. Separately ask product directors about the last product-data request. Record who worked, hours lost, deadline, budget owner and paid supplier before pitching.</li>
+<li><strong>Days 31–45:</strong> offer the €7,500 CRA baseline at one scope and price. Offer the €2,500 Data Act module only to the product director. Maximum pre-evidence spend is €5,000 for counsel review, insurance advice, travel, optional language support and a disposable prototype. Build no platform and hire nobody.</li>
+<li><strong>Days 46–75:</strong> deliver at most two paid CRA baselines in each customer's existing tools. Time every task and classify each decision as legal, manufacturer risk, implementation or routine operation. Run the incident clock. Test a product-data path only when its separate module is bought.</li>
+<li><strong>Days 76–90:</strong> ask each CRA buyer to sign a six-month managed-operation pilot at €3,000 monthly, billed in advance. Passing requires two paid baselines from ten qualified offers and at least one direct retainer. It also requires 60% of forecast recurring work to be analyst or engineer work. Kill after no paid baseline from ten qualified offers. Also kill after two baselines reveal less than one day monthly of recurring external work. If every qualified prospect requires Dutch-led delivery, stop the direct model and reassess it as a partner route.</li>
